    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** serving as our primary offensive engine. Boasting an elite 86.90 efficiency score, **Corbin Carroll** faces Walbert Ure\u00f1a in an ideal setup, as the combination of an favorable opposing xERA of 4.65 and an aggressive #2 spot in the lineup maximizes his elite speed for the scarcity-driven SB category. Complementing him is **James Wood**, whose 78.42 score against Mitch Spence is largely fueled by his elite 0.403 xwOBA and a prime lead-off spot. Both **Corbin Carroll** and **James Wood** are prioritized for their ability to catalyze our R and SB metrics against vulnerable right-handed arms.\n\nWe are navigating several lower-tier projections, particularly with **Zach McKinstry** (42.41) and **Alex Freeland** (52.50). **Zach McKinstry** is held in the lineup primarily for roster continuity, though he faces a significant handicap hitting 8th against Kai-Wei Teng. **Kyle Karros** presents an interesting case; while his base projection is modest, the combination of wind blowing out and a positive platoon edge against Shota Imanaga bumps him to a 51.84 score. **Dalton Rushing** was the closest call for the utility spot, ultimately edging out potential internal candidates by maintaining a 55.47 score despite the risks associated with Nick Martinez\u2019s repertoire.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given that every player\u2019s position is currently \"Lineup Pending.\" We are monitoring the status of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Tyler Soderstrom** closely, as any downward shift in their projected batting order could compress their scores below the 60.0 threshold. With **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Mickey Moniak** sidelined on the IL, and key utility depth like **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Cole Young**, **Carson Williams**, and **Travis Bazzana** currently seeing no game action, our roster flexibility is limited. We will monitor pre-game reports to ensure our projected lineup holds, particularly for **Max Muncy** and **Henry Bolte**, who remain startable but sit near the lower edge of our \"Strong\" efficiency band.",
